cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "prng-lattice-lab: recoverability of java.util.Random under partial-state leakage"
abstract: >-
  A closed, offline research harness that characterises the recoverability boundary of
  java.util.Random under partial-state leakage. Anchored on the Randar (Minecraft)
  truncated-LCG attack and generalised to a (bits-leaked-per-call x observations) phase
  diagram, with complete lattice and GF(2) solvers for the top-bits, nextInt(odd-bound),
  bit-length, and truncated-MT19937 leak models, and a fold-in seam to RepoAuditor as a
  weak_rng_adapter. Recovery demonstrations are reproducible and self-verifying.
type: software
authors:
  - name: erxxc
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/erxxc/prng-lattice-lab"
url: "https://github.com/erxxc/prng-lattice-lab"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - security
  - pseudo-random number generator
  - java.util.Random
  - linear congruential generator
  - mersenne twister
  - mt19937
  - lattice reduction
  - LLL
  - state recovery
  - predictable tokens
